# PERF-RADIX-1 inline key comparator — 2026-06-10 (issue #41 "try radix")
#
# Change: dedup_samples_packed_sort's comparator + merge-walk equality
# replaced with cmp_packed_key — big-endian u64-word lexicographic
# compare, inline, early-exit on the first differing word. The ORDERING
# FUNCTION is identical to <[u8;64]>::cmp (byte-wise memcmp), so pdqsort
# produces the identical permutation => byte-identical downstream,
# structurally. Kills the per-comparison libc __memcmp call (was
# 17.7%/10.0% of CPU on 12MP/1MP photos).
#
# Gates: bytes identical 4/4 A/B cells; hash-locks 36/36 default +
# parallel-tree-learning; lib 1488/1488; it 81/81; clippy clean.
#
# A/B (6 iters/side, loadavg 4.5 start / 3.8 end; base = item-2 binary,
# same lock):
#   clic097  -2.87% (min -1.5%)    city12mp -3.10% (mins ~equal)
#   terminal -1.84% (min -2.6%)    clic028 -12.03% — NOT citable: both
#   sides' spreads are bimodal (2.2-4.3 s); direction-only evidence.
# Read: consistent win, ~1/3 of the memcmp share recovered (the word
# loads remain; only call overhead + tail byte work removed).
#
# TRUE-RADIX (chunk 2) HONEST-STOP: an LSD/MSD radix produces a
# DIFFERENT permutation among equal keys; the sort is UNSTABLE and the
# equal-run representative's raw (unkeyed) fields flow into compaction,
# so representative choice is byte-relevant — a radix swap is NOT
# byte-safe without first proving the key covers every downstream-read
# field (or switching the walk to pick min-original-index
# representatives AND re-locking). Remaining sort cost is now dominated
# by the random-access key loads (keys[order[i]] indirection), which
# radix passes would multiply, not remove. Don't respawn without a
# locality redesign (e.g. sort (prefix, idx) pairs).
# Host: lilith (7950X, WSL2), no target-cpu=native.
